# Cloudflare Pages reads this from the deployed root.

# Pages caches responses at its own edge with a 7-day s-maxage that the zone
# purge API cannot reach. A redirect at a path is the one thing found to
# REPLACE a cached object there; deleting the page alone leaves Pages serving
# the old 200 for a week. Same pattern for /blog/ and /dad/.

# The blog is off again (config.extra.blog = false, content/blog drafted).
# Without these lines, parkerhunt.me/blog/ and the old posts keep answering
# from the pre-takedown deployment while the new one has no /blog at all.
/blog     /  301
/blog/    /  301
/blog/*   /  301

# /dad/ was published for a few hours and is now local only.
/dad      /  301
/dad/     /  301
/dad/*    /  301
